sorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","madeBy":"model","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_cd3120f7-030a-4af8-a6d1-28ecae789f1a","sessionId":"b575a9e5-080c-46d7-b71a-f5842e099a04","version":"2.1.330","gitBranch":"claude/misrouted-failures","slug":"linear-finding-kay-of-b575a9e5-080c-46d7-b71a-f5842e099a04","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"2e7fe753-0743-41c6-a544-23bed2d46bd4","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"72013b54-b18f-48cf-ab14-3227cd513d22","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LfHmc3LW8uu9P5bmLJatJM","type":"tool_result","content":"# Each misrouted failure: a simple change, or more (2026-11-25)\n\nRead only, on the app at `jusprin-dev` `9f485c3604` and the server at `master` `d9c224e114`. Nothing\nwas changed, built or run for this file. Each place in `error-handling-misrouted-failures.md` has one\nentry, except the two Kenneth marked \"Not to be fixed\": the 120-second limit on a reply, and a\ncheckout that returns \"succeeded\" with the invoice unpaid. The list's place 21 holds seven separate\nspots, and its places 26 and 27 hold two and four. Each of those spots has its own entry, so there are\n50 entries in all. App paths are under `src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/`, server paths under `web_ent/jusprin/`.\n\n\"Simple\" here is the reading in the brief, not Kenneth's wording. The change is made at the place\nitself by adding or removing a try/catch or an if/else, or by deleting handling. It uses only what the\ncode has today.\n\n## Counts\n\n- **Simple: 17.**\n- **Needs more: 30.**\n- **Nothing to change: 3.**\n- **Never made to happen: 34.** This counts across the three groups above. It means the failure\n  itself was never produced against the real thing, by me or in the evidence I have. A test with a\n  fake counts as never made to happen.\n\nThe most common reasons a place needs more:\n- the person's failure can only be told to them with words we do not have: a new sentence, or the\n  \"the system says\" frame that went with the reversal;\n- the failure repeats, every few seconds or on every press, so reporting it once needs a record of\n  what was already reported;\n- the page or callback gets only \"worked or not\", so telling \"ours\" apart from \"no network\" needs a\n  new field.\n\n## The app\n\n**Credits and plans, Billing and usage, will not open.**\n- Where: `Shell/ServerSheet.cpp:86-96`, the answer to the link request. Any answer other than 200 with a\n  link, or no answer, shows \"Couldn't load Credits and plans\" (`:375`) with \"Check your internet\n  connection, then try again.\"\n- Whose: an error answer from our server is ours, and no answer is the person's network. An ended\n  sign-in (401) is the person's. Never made to happen.\n- Change: throw on an error answer inside the existing `reported(...)` callback, and keep the sentence\n  for no answer.\n14:## Counts\n31:## The app\n332:## The server","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"1a2c61d3-465a-4d19-ae2a-08f3bba20fc1","timestamp":"2026-11-25T18:39:40.447Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"# Each misrouted failure: a simple change, or more (2026-11-25)\n\nRead only, on the app at `jusprin-dev` `9f485c3604` and the server at `master` `d9c224e114`. Nothing\nwas changed, built or run for this file. Each place in `error-handling-misrouted-failures.md` has one\nentry, except the two Kenneth marked \"Not to be fixed\": the 120-second limit on a reply, and a\ncheckout that returns \"succeeded\" with the invoice unpaid. The list's place 21 holds seven separate\nspots, and its places 26 and 27 hold two and four. Each of those spots has its own entry, so there are\n50 entries in all. App paths are under `src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/`, server paths under `web_ent/jusprin/`.\n\n\"Simple\" here is the reading in the brief, not Kenneth's wording. The change is made at the place\nitself by adding or removing a try/catch or an if/else, or by deleting handling. It uses only what the\ncode has today.\n\n## Counts\n\n- **Simple: 17.**\n- **Needs more: 30.**\n- **Nothing to change: 3.**\n- **Never made to happen: 34.** This counts across the three groups above. It means the failure\n  itself was never produced against the real thing, by me or in the evidence I have. A test with a\n  fake counts as never made to happen.\n\nThe most common reasons a place needs more:\n- the person's failure can only be told to them with words we do not have: a new sentence, or the\n  \"the system says\" frame that went with the reversal;\n- the failure repeats, every few seconds or on every press, so reporting it once needs a record of\n  what was already reported;\n- the page or callback gets only \"worked or not\", so telling \"ours\" apart from \"no network\" needs a\n  new field.\n\n## The app\n\n**Credits and plans, Billing and usage, will not open.**\n- Where: `Shell/ServerSheet.cpp:86-96`, the answer to the link request. Any answer other than 200 with a\n  link, or no answer, shows \"Couldn't load Credits and plans\" (`:375`) with \"Check your internet\n  connection, then try again.\"\n- Whose: an error answer from our server is ours, and no answer is the person's network. An ended\n  sign-in (401) is the person's. Never made to happen.\n- Change: throw on an error answer inside the existing `reported(...)` callback, and keep the sentence\n  for no answer.\n14:## Counts\n31:## The app\n332:## The server","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2e7fe753-0743-41c6-a544-23bed2d46bd4","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_cd3120f7-030a-4af8-a6d1-28ecae789f1a","sessionId":"b575a9e5-080c-46d7-b71a-f5842e099a04","version":"2.1.330","gitBranch":"claude/misrouted-failures","slug":"linear-finding-kay-of-b575a9e5-080c-46d7-b71a-f5842e099a04","dataFlowOn":true}
